      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A perusal of the custody certificate further reveals that the petitioners are not involved in any other criminal cases."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b104a86c6b8d4db8bba0064c16569e0a_39",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "ANALYSIS 5."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ae516b305d414042a0b955e3f65a3de0_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n6. \"Bail is the Rule and Jail is an Exception\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "07bc1d917a8c4131bdf1de271943580e_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This basic principle of criminal jurisprudence was laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court, way back in 3 of 9 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:097558 CRM-M-43352-2023 - 4- 1978, in its landmark judgment titled \"State of Rajasthan V. Balchand "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6225a8166caf4b47b26d40014285f998_43",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This principle finds its roots in one of the most distinguished fundamental rights, as enshrined in Article 21 of the Constitution of India."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "966ee455b81a4249bcc8ec1c5f4b8cd1_44",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Though the underlying objective behind detention of a person is to ensure easy availability of an accused for trial, without any inconvenience, however, in case the presence of an accused can be secured otherwise, then detention is not comp"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8e38af8189dc4e208fbd8da08dad8d64_45",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "7. The right to a speedy trial is one of the rights of a detained person."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "167b6046f1804211935f5c1bd0e4bbbd_46",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, while deciding application for regular bail, the Courts shall also take into consideration the fundamental precept of criminal jurisprudence, which is \"the presumption of innocence\", besides the gravity of offence(s)\ninvolved."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "718820ada8b743ea9a90d7b56a7c1bc6_47",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "8. In \"Gurbaksh Singh Sibbia v. State of Punjab\", (1980) 2 SCC 565 at 586-588, the purpose of granting bail is set out by the Hon'ble Supreme Court with great felicity as follows:-\n\"27."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "45e6fb73a881446a9149b5c525af69a9_48",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not necessary to refer to decisions which deal with the right to ordinary bail because that right does not furnish an exact parallel to the right to anticipatory bail."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "73d1660f0dd04c5ba3ad9458f101624a_49",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt is, however, interesting that as long back as in 1924 it was held by the High Court of Calcutta in Nagendra v. King Emperor, AIR 1924 Calcutta 476 (479, 480) that the object of bail is to secure the attendance of the accused at the tria"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ecf009edb8af43809bae1aeb4bd2b42b_50",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In two other cases which, significantly, are the 'Meerut Conspiracy cases observations are to be found regarding the right to bail which deserve a special mention."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5d64505cc9f5443d8f50158ca30003fe_51",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In K.N. Joglekar v.\nEmperor, AIR 1931 Allahabad 504 (SB) it was observed, while dealing with Section 498 which corresponds to the present Section 439 of the Code, that it 4 of 9 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:097558 CRM-M-43352-2023 - 5- co"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bb833db1a43645caa99fb1bb30c10bdc_52",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was observed by the Court that there was no hard and fast rule and no inflexible principle governing the exercise of the discretion conferred by Section 498 and that the only principle which was established was that the discretion should"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "93597dc49ca24cb78c8ab519ee1f2dca_53",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Emperor v. H.L. Hutchinson, AIR 1931 Allahabad 356 at p.\n358 it was said that it was very unwise to make an attempt to lay down any particular rules which bind the High Court, having regard to the fact that the legislature itself left th"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "812a051e313c4f0abb59f64dd0137b6e_54",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "According to the High Court, the variety of cases that may arise from time to time cannot be safely classified and it is dangerous to make an attempt to classify the cases and to say that in particular classes a bail may be granted but not "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "537d26ce9a634e4997dd7c818c44c9c8_55",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was observed that the principle to be deduced from the various sections in the Criminal Procedure Code was that grant of bail is the rule and refusal is the exception."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2598f875621f465aa797782ecf2bdd7b_56",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "An accused person who enjoys freedom is in a much better position to look after his case and to properly defend himself than if he were in custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5917a4db9f1f437786acb5cdddbd2bb6_57",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As a presumably innocent person he is therefore entitled to freedom and every opportunity to look after his own case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "718601bb9f4041c2a6c6b5e326d15b31_58",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A presumably innocent person must have his freedom to enable him to establish his innocence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2be381ef8c9944d3a999c3161e0a8463_59",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "XX XX XX 29."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5d719c59e86c4ac7a6234f0486f7d16f_60",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Gurcharan Singh v. State (Delhi Admn.) (1978) 1 SCC 118 it was observed by Goswami, J., who spoke for the Court, that \"there cannot be an inexorable formula in the matter of granting bail."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e6e0942305d9477b9c9b943e48e8cea4_61",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The facts and circumstances of each case will govern the exercise of judicial discretion in granting or cancelling bail\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "320582088a1c45078fb800423c98705a_62",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "30. In American Jurisprudence (2d, Vol. 8, page 806, para 39) it is stated :\n\"Where the granting of bail lies within the discretion of the court, the granting or denial is regulated, to a large extent, by the facts and circumstances of each"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "58615c76325a4f18b97b7f6e55e783bc_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since 5 of 9 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:097558 CRM-M-43352-2023 - 6- the object of the detention or imprisonment of the accused is to secure his appearance and submission to the jurisdiction and the judgment of the court, the Kameshar R"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6a160de047f54e719cf57c96d5470052_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "primary inquiry is whether a recognizance or bond would effect that end.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "80d75f93f9204e2b9dafa8ea69966b9d_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nIt is thus clear that the question whether to grant bail or not depends for its answer upon a variety of circumstances, the cumulative effect of which must enter into the judicial verdict."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b127ded273334dcd96c06c7ed923a35d_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Any one single circumstance cannot be treated as of universal validity or as necessarily justifying the grant or refusal of bail.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "661fa5f722574667895ffe3c19e28a22_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "9. Also, in \"Gudikanti Narasimhulu and others Versus Public Prosecutor, High Court of Andhra Pradesh\", 1978 AIR (Supreme Court) 429, the Hon'ble Supreme Court, speaking through Krishna Iyer, J., has enunciated the principles of bail thus :\n"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5640e60602014952b4f8c7b8917dc00b_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus the legal principle and practice validate the court considering the likelihood of the applicant interfering with witnesses for the prosecution or otherwise polluting the process of justice."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5b974eae8703447689296d8b55dd1dd6_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not only traditional but rational, in this context, to enquire into the antecedents of a man who is applying for bail to find whether he has a bad record-particularly a record which suggests that he is likely to commit serious offence"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ae7cf58bae7d4e3e99eeac3c881dfb0e_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In regard to habitual, it is part of criminological history that a thoughtless bail order has enabled the bailee to exploit the opportunity to inflict further crimes on the member of society."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c8328cd1d6b446f9bc3fc4a45fb65596_71",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Bail discretion, on the basis of evidence about the criminal record of a defendant, is therefore not an exercise in irrelevance."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9c3aadf355a04a42ba0fec351ff614d5_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "10. The significance and sweep of Article 21 make the deprivation of liberty a matter of grave concern and permissible only when the law authorising it is reasonable,\neven-handed and geared to he goals of community good and State necessity "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "508f1291504d448e99f5d9554084df0d_73",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Indeed, the considerations I have set out as criteria are germane to the constitutional proposition I have deduced."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "99dce80b095040e19c8c3f90962679e1_74",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Reasonableness postulates intelligent care and predicates that deprivation of freedom by refusal of bail is not for punitive purpose but for the bi- 6 of 9 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:097558 CRM-M-43352-2023 - 7- focal interests of justi"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d1f4bf2de1604ceab096d798c4da2546_75",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n11. We must weight the contrary factors to answer the test the reasonableness, subject to the need for securing the presence of the bail applicant."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "86eee11e0f2e4cd999a4d2614678586a_76",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It makes sense to assume that a man on bail has a better chance to prepare of present his case than one remanded in custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d74e031551ff44438dbe2928a617188a_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "And if public justice is to be promoted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a7eb3e5887d74945a0c5d520eb731400_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "mechanical detention should be demoted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4148818bede74267a4356948bf7cee2d_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the United States, which has a constitutional perspective close to ours, the function of bail is limited, 'community roots' of the applicant are stressed and, after the Vera Foundation's Manhattan Bail Project, monetary suretyship is los"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "68730edb5c36469995897bf313c45c86_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The considerable public expense in keeping in custody where no danger of disappearance or disturbance can arise, is not a negligible consideration."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f11adf97f4d54d48a85c8a979ae127fb_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nEqually important is the deplorable condition, verging on the inhuman, of our sub-jails, that the unrewarding cruelty and expensive custody of avoidable Kameshar Rai @ Kameshwar Rai And Anr vs State Of Punjab on 31 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "231dfe444e934ac6be09f0610b99e90a_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n5 incarceration makes refusal of bail unreasonable and a policy favouring release justly sensible."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7cd32830afc9491cbb16080b69a6d7dc_83",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n12. A few other weighty factors deserve reference."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dee3793193274fd6aef00a3608f3ccd6_84",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "All deprivation of liberty is validated by social defence and individual correction along an anti-criminal direction."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a3413bb0156b40bfbc09ef1394bebcc6_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nPublic justice is central to the whole scheme of bail law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1b26b471b91a43128911e15edd2231c1_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Fleeing justice must be forbidden but punitive harshness should be minimised."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "92270042a2144992b1b907dd92319785_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Restorative devices to redeem the man, even through community service, meditative drill, study classes or other resources should be innovated, and playing foul with public peace by tampering with evidence, intimidating witnesses or committi"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6ad8f36ee65f4f74b020e966bddc1640_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No seeker of justice shall play confidence tricks on the court or community."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "989bddc9801047ccb71a23d67dfcabd3_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, conditions may be hung around bail orders, not to cripple but to protect."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "60ee466a12c34e09b7388e56ccd7db6e_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Such is the holistic jurisdiction and humanistic orientation invoked by the judicial discretion correlated to the values of our Constitution."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1c0c01587b5b45f7bafa5a7683649b13_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
